---
import { link, site } from '../config.mjs';
import CountryGuides from './CountryGuides.astro';
import LearningArtwork from './LearningArtwork.astro';
import GuideCards from './GuideCards.astro';
import { gradeGuides } from '../data/guides.mjs';
---
<section class="section wrap reading-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">ONLINE TUITION FOR NRI STUDENTS</p><h2>Start with the child.<br/><em>Then make the plan.</em></h2><LearningArtwork scene="family-curiosity" caption="Curiosity feels at home, anywhere."/></div><div class="prose"><p>Living abroad can mean navigating a new school system, staying with an Indian curriculum or preparing for another move. A useful tuition plan begins by separating those goals. Which subject needs support now, and which future question can wait?</p><p>Friction Classes offers one-on-one online learning for Classes 1–9 in Maths, Science, English, and Coding and Logical Thinking. Our mentors are engineering students and mentors from top institutions such as IIT Madras and NSUT. We discuss subject fit and availability before confirming a match.</p><h3>Make the school’s work the starting point</h3><p>Share the school programme, current topics and a task your child finds difficult. Lessons are aligned to your child’s curriculum, including {site.curricula.join(', ')}. We confirm topic coverage rather than assuming that a country, grade number or curriculum label tells the whole story.</p><p>A child might need a concept explained differently, practice writing a clear answer, or help connecting familiar ideas to a new method. Those needs call for different lessons. A gentle level check and a conversation with the family help identify a sensible starting point.</p></div></section>
<section class="section wrap values-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">ONE LEARNER</p><h2 class="guide-h2">A lesson that can pause</h2><p>One-on-one attention gives a mentor room to revisit a step, ask about the learner’s thinking and check a new example. The aim is understanding and growing independence, not completing school assignments for the child.</p><a class="text-link" href={link('learn/why-one-on-one-tuition/')}>How one-on-one support can help ↗</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">A REALISTIC WEEK</p><h2 class="guide-h2">Overlap is only the beginning</h2><p>Start with sleep, school and family commitments, then discuss possible class windows. Some families prefer weekends; others can fit a weekday routine. We confirm the city, date and local time together, including seasonal clock changes.</p><a class="text-link" href={link('learn/study-routines-across-time-zones/')}>Build a routine across time zones ↗</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">A PARENT PARTNERSHIP</p><h2 class="guide-h2">Updates with a next step</h2><p>Ask what your child can explain independently, where prompts are still needed and what comes next. Share school feedback so the plan stays relevant. Progress varies, and no particular mark or outcome is promised.</p><a class="text-link" href={link('learn/understanding-learning-progress/')}>Ask useful questions about progress ↗</a></article></section>
<CountryGuides/>
<section class="section wrap"><p class="eyebrow">CLASSES 1–9</p><h2>Support for their<br/><em>stage of learning.</em></h2><GuideCards items={gradeGuides.map(guide => ({title:guide.title,description:guide.intro,path:`programs/${guide.slug}/`}))}/></section>
<section class="section wrap narrow prose"><h2>Before the first conversation</h2><p>Have the child’s class, curriculum, subject and preferred local times ready. A recent topic list or a description of the difficulty can help; you do not need to send sensitive school records in an enquiry.</p><p>Ask about the mentor, the demo format, parent communication and the plan’s terms. A WhatsApp enquiry is the start of a discussion, not a confirmed booking. Message us for a personalized plan.</p><p>If your family is planning a move, read our <a href={link('learn/switching-school-curricula/')}>curriculum-change checklist</a> and ask the receiving school about placement. We support learning; we do not decide admissions or grade equivalence.</p></section>
